(* gap_witness2 (proofs.v l.3786-3800): X0 ^= =? X1 X2 in neq_store.
   neq_store = nil_store with X2 = (nil.nil); it is built by the first
   assignment (X3 = X4 = nil, so =? X3 X4 is t).  X1 <> X2, so the
   right-hand side is nil while X0 is nil: both printed ss assignment
   rules are blocked, the printed ds and the repaired rules leave the
   store unchanged.  Expected output: (nil.nil) (the value of X2). *)
  X2 ^= =? X3 X4;
  X0 ^= =? X1 X2;
